# UI

Prefer a daisyUI component over raw CSS. Use Tailwind utilities for layout and spacing. Tailwind v4 is loaded by `@tailwindcss/vite`; tokens live in `src/style.css`. Leave `tailwind.config.js` and component `<style>` blocks out unless no daisyUI or Tailwind class exists.

## daisyUI

- Buttons: `btn btn-primary`, `btn btn-outline`, `btn btn-ghost`. Set `type="button"` on buttons that do not submit a form.
- Choices: `checkbox checkbox-primary` or `radio radio-primary` inside `fieldset` and `fieldset-label`.
- Surfaces: `rounded-box border border-base-300 bg-base-100`.
- Groups: `join` with `join-item`. Navigation: `navbar`.

## Color

Use semantic theme colors (`bg-base-100`, `text-base-content`, `border-error`, `btn-primary`). Change the palette only in the `discovery` block in `src/style.css`.

```vue
<button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" @click="emit('next')">Continue</button>
```

Put shared element styles in `@layer base` in `src/style.css`. Component files style through the `class` attribute.
